TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The intro (which also repeats between verses) is three strums of (G) and one strum of (C).  Then from the (C) add your pinky to the 1st string (like you're playing a (CaddG)).  Now pluck the 2nd string, the covered bottom string, the 2nd string again, and lift off all but the pinky and slide the pinky up to the 5th fret and pluck the covered bottom string.  Repeat 3 more times, do just the chords again and begin the song.  Try it, it's really pretty easy. 
 
 
